    "chunk_text": "23. It is an offense to maintain premises without a license to be obtained under this by-law or in violation of any of the provisions of the by-law. (2) Subject to a fine referred to in subSection (2). When a person who has been convicted of an offense continues to pursue such violation or violation, a written notice shall be given by the\n\nChairman, the Medical Officer of Health or the Public Health Inspector. Each day the violation continues after receiving Promotion are subject to the above said article and an additional fine.\n\n24. Unless otherwise required in this By-Law,\n\n\"Chairman\" shall mean the person holding the office of the Chairman of the Pradeshiya Sabha at the moment\n\nor performing the functions of that office.\n\n\"Pradeshiya Sabha\" shall mean Kuruwita Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n\" Medical Officer\" shall mean the person holding the office of any Medical Officer of Health in the area of the\n\nDivisional Council area.\n\n\"Public Health Inspector\" shall mean the person holding the office of any Public Health Inspector in the area\n\nof the Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n\"Authorized officer\" shall mean any officer authorized by the Chairman at the moment,\n\n\"Licensee\" shall mean an organization, person or person licensed under this by-law;\n\nReducing the amount of microorganisms in the environment through chemical agents or physical means to a\n\nlevel that does not reduce the safety or appropriateness of the \"disinfectant\";\n\n\"Drinking water\" shall mean water that does not contain enough pollutants and causes bacterial and chemical\n\nconditions that meet the national standards for causing disease or physical harm;\n\n\"Reasonable Time\" shall mean the Licensed Function or the relevant time.\n\n25. If there is any inconsistency between the Sinhala, Tamil and English texts of this by-law, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nFirst Schedule\n\nApplication for obtaining a trade license for the year \u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2