    "chunk_text": "12. Where a stone quarry or crusher where a license has been issued under the by-laws of this section is in violation of the provisions of section 7 of this by-law, the premises shall comply with all such requirements before the specified date a notice to the Licensee shall be delivered by the Chairman that should make the maximum time that should not exceed 30 days.\n\n14. In the event that any licensee who has received a notice in terms of section 12 of this by-law has failed to act in the manner specified in that notice or before the date on which such notice is extended, the license issued to the relevant place shall be revoked by the Chairman. It must be legal.\n\n15. It is an offense to maintain premises without a license to be obtained under this by-law or to violate any of the provisions of the by-law and after being convicted by a court of competent jurisdiction for such offense, 122 of the Pradeshiya Sabha Act No.15 of 1987 (2) Subject to a fine referred to in subsection (2). When a violation or violation is continued by a person who has been found guilty of an offense by a court of competent jurisdiction over the offense, a written notice shall be given by the Chairman or the Medical Officer of Health, Public Health Inspector. Each subsequent violation continues An additional fine of the above section shall also be imposed for a fine.\n\n16. Unless otherwise required in the by-laws;\n\n\"Chairman\" means the person holding the office of Chairman of this Pradeshiya Sabha or performing the functions of that office.\n\n\"Pradeshiya Sabha\" shall mean Nivithigala Pradeshiya Sabha\n\n\" Medical Officer of Health \" shall mean the person holding the office of any Medical Officer of Health in the area of the Pradeshiya Sabha area.\n\n\"Public Health Inspector\" shall mean the person holding the office of any Public Health Inspector in the area of the Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n\"Authorized officer\" shall mean any officer authorized by the Chairman 